{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Cakes of matzot.</b> A flat loaf of matzah; dough that has not leavened is called matzah." "<b>And also provisions they did not make for themselves.</b> For the road. This tells Israel's praise — that they did not say, 'How shall we go out into the wilderness without provisions?' Rather, they believed and went. So it is expounded in the tradition: ״זָכַרְתִּי לָךְ חֶסֶד נְעוּרַיִךְ אַהֲבַת כְּלוּלֹתָיִךְ לֶכְתֵּךְ אַחֲרַי בַּמִּדְבָּר בְּאֶרֶץ לֹא זְרוּעָה״ (Jeremiah 2). What reward is explicitly stated after it? ״קֹדֶשׁ יִשְׂרָאֵל לַה׳ וגו׳״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:50.414120735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}